index=* EventCode=4625
| stats count dc(Account_Name) as targeted_accounts values(Account_Name) as accounts by Source_Network_Address
| where targeted_accounts >= 3
| sort - targeted_accounts


What this is doing

Your report says the important indicator wasn't just one failed login. It was one source generating failed authentication attempts against multiple accounts within a short period, which is exactly the behavior we're trying to summarize here.

This query:

EventCode=4625

looks for:

Failed Windows logons.

Then:

dc(Account_Name)

means:

Count the number of distinct accounts targeted.

Then:

by Source_Network_Address

groups everything by the machine/IP that generated the authentication attempts.

And:

where targeted_accounts >= 3

shows sources targeting at least three different accounts.
